Hi folks, as some of you probably figured from my questions over the
last few weeks, I'm pretty new to Nethack. Started my first game in
August (so maybe 6 weeks ago?) so I'm pretty pleased I've managed to
ascend :) This is my 32nd character, mostly
Valkyries (bar the odd failed experiment with a few wizards and
rangers). This is also the first game I've ever passed the stage where
I had the mines and sokoban both completed.

Quick note on this.. the middle game was pretty easy. I died over and
over at the beginning (as you can see from my top
score chart down below, I'd never scored over 55k points in a game
heh) but as soon as I got passed it, well, here is the post :)

So, the ascension. I notice alot of people have, how would I put them,
'house rules'? that they adhere to themselves that aren't inherently
built in to the game. Like, some people don't like spoilers for
example. Beyond the obvious (not save scumming, reloading games or any
of that crap) I don't like to play with bones files. I find it's a
little unfair to bump into a full ascension kit. Seems a bit silly to
me, but hey.

Won't bore you with all the details, just want to point out a few bits
I found interesting.

I used daggers as my weapon of choice for a long time, even getting to
the point where I was two weaponing two magic daggers before I had
even raised another skill. Wasn't sure which of excalibur or mjollnir
I'd get first (ended up being mjollnir, which I wielded alongside a
shield for the entire game).

Once the mines were done, the game got pretty easy. By the time I hit
the castle I had a pretty good AC, and could just stand in doorways
and maul through crowds, barely ever losing HP. I guess this is why
alot of people ascend with valkyries first. They're pretty tough, I
don't think I was ever in danger of dying.. I got surrounded by some
pretty serious crowds at a few points and could just splatter my way
through them.

Made a few mistakes in the middle.. got drowned by an eel twice
(genocided the things after the second time). An abundance of life
saving amulets made this ok though. Found 3 and wished for another in
the end. Also genocided L and M at this point to make it easier for
myself.

Gehennom is pretty dull.. was looking forward to going toe to toe with
the demon lords but they all went down in about three hits. Orcus was
fun, burrowed down to the level below and came out wielding a
cockatrice. Wand of death with full charges came in real handy later
on (although I wish now I'd saved some charging scrolls for them.. I
wasted them all on markers getting my armour properly enchanted).

Once I found the square, enchanted my stuff as much as I could and
filled my backpack with various wands and potions, I bombed down to
the wizard and slapped him. Turns out I'd have to kill him 9 times in
the end.. he was a serious pain in the ass. Went through two wands of
death on him before I was reduced to beating him in the face over and
over. He summoned a few crowds, stole the amulet once, but a quick
teleport and mjollnir to the face sorts him out :)

Going up to the planes was pretty easy. Bar a few annoying mysterious
forces putting me miles away from stairs with no energy, I think
probably 30 of the levels.. literally nothing happened bar bumping
into the odd fox I'd left behind earlier. The planes was a new
experience for me, knowing you can't go back makes it pretty exciting
I think. Found the earth portal in the last room after spamming away a
load of digging wands. This plane was easy to be honest, once I beat
down the wizard  it was just a case of finding the portal.

Air was easy, put on a conflict ring and just pelted it to the portal.

Fire was, for me, the worst part of the whole game. I got really,
really sick of scrolling through fire elementals wandering through
fire traps. Seriously, I don't care.. I can see the trap and the
monster on the map, I know what they both are, I don't need to know
every single time they don't get affected :P Took a while but found
the portal without killing anything (conflict was fun here).

Water was real easy. Used the Orb of Fate, levitated to the portal,
entered. Easy!

Astral was the most fun part of nethack for me, I think. Loads of hard
monsters ( I say hard, I wasn't in much danger but it was fun watching
them all rage around attacking each other). Wandered over to the right
to face Death, turned out to be the neutral temple. killed death a few
times with mjollnir, he's pretty weak!

Went middle next, and Pestilence. Had a large potion stock and 2
unihorns so I figured he'd be easy. Other than a bunch of random
monsters that got summoned (hence the odd genocides at the end :p) it
was pretty easy. Zapped teleport, moved up, repeat. Found the lawful
altar and boom, demigoddess!

Spent the majority of my time prepared for the ascension run. Seems I
wasted my time, as you can see from the massive list of stuff I
brought in my bag, would have been better off just keeping a couple of
tele and dig wands, a whole bunch of healing potions and holy water
and just leading with mjollnir.

Want to say thanks alot to you guys, those of you who helped me out
really really helped me with this, and the discussions on the groups
about the technicalities of the game really spurred me on to finish
it :)

Will attempt a cavemen ascension next I think :) Probably work through
all the melee characters, then once I'm happy with those, start on the
casters.


